    "body": "Actually one intricate way where this is currently observable is the `onload` of the link element. It's unclear when it's supposed to fire if we're using a resource-type-specific cache. For images should it be fired only after the image is decoded? For scripts only after the script is executed? Hence the response cloning, which could be implemented in other more optimized ways of course (but guarantees the observable behavior of the link's `load` event)\r\n.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
